#
# The audio policy configuration.
#
# The stock /vendor/etc/audio_policy_configuration.xml gives the Bluetooth SCO
# headset microphone, an input, an output channel mask. Our copy, with that
# mask corrected, is mounted over the vendor's before audioserver starts with
# class core on boot; the files it includes are still found next to it in
# /vendor/etc. Only audioserver reads it -- no vendor library or service names
# the file -- so it keeps the label of the rest of /system/etc. The vendor
# image stays as it is.
on post-fs
    mount none /system/etc/audio_policy_configuration.xml /vendor/etc/audio_policy_configuration.xml bind
